    "result": "I implemented both functions in `solution.py` and wrote 30 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 30. `can_book` runs the spec's checks in order: the two `ValueError`s first, then same-day, the 4-hour limit (inclusive), opening and closing hours (inclusive), and finally the conflict test with buffer. The conflict test is `start >= existing_end + buffer or end <= existing_start - buffer`, which covers the half-open and back-to-back cases. `merge_intervals` validates every interval, sorts a copy by start, and merges when `start <= previous_end`, so touching intervals merge too. The tests cover each rule's boundaries, the buffer edges, unsorted and chained merges, and non-mutation of the input. I did not run coverage, since only the pytest command was allowed, but the tests exercise every branch in `solution.py`, so the 90% gate should pass.",
